  "details": "I like to put music or ambient noises and other stuff on my avatars.\n\nThe sounds have never broken for me myself, but...\n\nBut I often get other people saying the audio is coming out broken and people have sent me video clips of how choppy and bad it is.\n\nOther times someone will come to me from across the world and mention how someone is playing world audio, even though I often set the max distances all to 10, instead of the default 40 which actually does cover the size of most worlds.\n\nI have many past avatars that used to have functioning audio, which at some point regressed without me reuploading them, and had their audio broken in the same way.\n\nBut even making just a new avatar and putting some kind of toggle-music on, causes this anyway.\n\nI'm using just the default vrc spatial audio source with the audio source component.\n\nI'm animating the audio source component from off to on to enable the music, as recommended in the documentation, and I'm not animating the gameobject it's on.",
